{
  "company_name": "PlanWorks Manufacturing",
  "industry": "Machinery",
  "use_case": "Manufacturing resource planning and capacity optimization",
  "space_title": "PlanWorks Manufacturing - Resource Planning 🏭",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Machinery\n\n**Use case:** Manufacturing Resource Planning & Capacity Optimization\n\nPlanWorks Manufacturing — MRP and finite capacity analytics across work centers and routings. Production Planners and Schedulers manage work-order release and queue position daily; the VP Operations and CFO use it to balance load vs capacity, drive schedule adherence, and reduce overtime spend without missing customer commitments.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Schedule adherence (%) — target ≥90%\n- Capacity utilization (%) — sweet spot 80–90%, >95% triggers expedite/overtime\n- On-time work order completion (%) — target ≥95%\n- Throughput (units) — capacity output indicator\n- Efficiency (%) — actual vs standard hours, target ≥90%\n- Overtime hours — cost and worker-burnout signal\n- Changeover hours — SMED/lean improvement opportunity\n- Queue hours — bottleneck and lead-time driver\n\n**Data sources**\n- `work_orders` — work-order records with planned vs actual hours, completed quantity, status, priority\n- `capacity_snapshots` — weekly available/loaded hours, utilization, queue depth, overtime, headcount\n- `planning_kpi_monthly` — monthly schedule adherence, throughput, efficiency, on-time, scrap, changeover",
  "schema_basename": "mach_mrp",
